# Pinned versions of the components the devnet runs against.
#
# The chain builds from this repository; everything else it needs is a released
# artefact from another repository, pinned here rather than built from a sibling
# checkout. That is the whole point of the split: the devnet exercises the same
# artefacts an operator would run, not whatever happens to be in a neighbouring
# working tree.
#
# Both have a local-build escape hatch for cross-repo development, which is the
# one case where you *do* want the sibling checkout:
#
#   make dev-up   GUARDIAND_BIN=~/dev/timeflareio/guardian/bin/guardiand
#   make e2e      SDK_DIR=~/dev/timeflareio/typescript-sdk
#
# Bump these deliberately: a version here is a claim about what the chain is
# known to work with, and it feeds COMPATIBILITY.md.

# github.com/timeflareio/guardian — release providing guardiand binaries.
GUARDIAN_VERSION=v0.0.3

# github.com/timeflareio/typescript-sdk — release providing the SDK dist
# tarball that drives the e2e suites.
#
# The EXAMPLES bundle from this release drives the e2e harness. The same release
# also publishes a dist-only tarball for consumers that vendor the package; that
# one has no examples/ and is not what the devnet wants.
SDK_VERSION=v0.0.2
